---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Queenstown Trip — New Zealand</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page" id="top">
      <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
      <header class="site-header">
        <a class="site-title" href="/">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.7" />
            <path d="M12 1L14 10L23 12L14 14L12 23L10 14L1 12L10 10Z" fill="currentColor" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.7" fill="var(--paper)" />
          </svg>
          New Zealand
        </a>
      </header>

      <div class="hero">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">South Island, New Zealand</p>
          <h1>Queenstown</h1>
          <p class="hero-date">11–18 October 2026</p>
        </div>
        <img
          class="locator"
          src="/new-zealand.svg"
          width="256"
          height="312"
          alt="New Zealand, with Queenstown marked on the South Island."
        />
      </div>

      <p>Seven of us, one week in Queenstown. This is our plan for mountain walks, good food, and time together, with room to change our minds.</p>

      <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Trip sections">
        <a href="#overview">The trip</a>
        <a href="#accommodation">Stay</a>
        <a href="#major-activities">Activities</a>
        <a href="#schedule">The week</a>
        <a href="#to-confirm">To do</a>
        <a href="#other-suggestions">Other suggestions</a>
      </nav>

      <main id="main">
        <PlanSection number="01" headingId="overview" title="The Trip">
          <dl class="trip-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>Base</dt>
              <dd>Queenstown</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Flying from</dt>
              <dd>Melbourne</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>The group</dt>
              <dd>7 people</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p>A few planned activities, two hikes, and plenty of time for pubs, food, and doing nothing. No car except for the Glenorchy road-trip day.</p>
          <div class="flight-notes">
            <p>
              <strong>Sunday 11 October · Jetstar JQ219</strong><br />
              Melbourne Tullamarine <time datetime="2026-10-11T14:50:00+11:00">2:50 PM</time>
              → Queenstown <time datetime="2026-10-11T20:00:00+13:00">8:00 PM</time>
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Sunday 18 October · Jetstar JQ220</strong><br />
              Queenstown <time datetime="2026-10-18T12:10:00+13:00">12:10 PM</time>
              → Melbourne Tullamarine <time datetime="2026-10-18T13:35:00+11:00">1:35 PM</time>
            </p>
            <p class="note">All times local. Melbourne flights use T2 International.</p>
          </div>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="02" headingId="accommodation" title="Accommodation">
          <p class="activity-meta">Booked · 7 nights</p>
          <h3><a href="https://www.airbnb.com.au/rooms/1248805245374389085">Modern Spacious Family Holiday Home</a></h3>
          <p class="note">Entire home · Hosted by Hello Queenstown</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=3%20Saint%20Peters%20Place%2C%20Queenstown%2C%20Otago%209300%2C%20New%20Zealand">3 Saint Peters Place, Queenstown, Otago 9300, New Zealand</a></p>
          <dl class="trip-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>Check-in</dt>
              <dd><time datetime="2026-10-11T15:00:00+13:00">11 Oct, from 3:00 PM</time></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Checkout</dt>
              <dd><time datetime="2026-10-18T10:00:00+13:00">18 Oct, by 10:00 AM</time></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Rooms</dt>
              <dd>4 bedrooms<br />5 beds</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p>Self check-in with a key safe. Wi-Fi, kitchen, washer, dryer, and free garage parking.</p>
          <p class="note" data-comment-anchor="bedroom-setup">Send the bedroom 3 setup choice to Hello Queenstown by 8 October. Changes after arrival cost NZ$100 per bed plus a NZ$10 call-out fee.</p>
          <p class="note">Non-refundable booking.</p>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="03" headingId="rough-plan" title="The Rough Plan">
          <ul class="rough-list">
            <li>2–3 larger activities</li>
            <li>2 local hikes</li>
            <li>1 wine half-day</li>
            <li>Onsen / hot pools</li>
          </ul>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="04" headingId="major-activities" title="Major Activity Ideas">

          <PlanSection id="glenorchy" headingAnchor="glenorchy" title="Glenorchy Road Trip">
            <span class="activity-meta" slot="meta">Full day</span>
            <p>Aim for Saturday 17 October. Monday 12 or Friday 16 are alternatives if the weather is better.</p>
            <p><strong>One-day rental:</strong> <a href="https://www.gorentals.co.nz/vehicles/van-or-people-carriers/">GO Rentals Kia Carnival Hybrid</a>, eight seats.</p>
            <ul data-comment-anchor="glenorchy-rental">
              <li><strong>NZ$302 total with Basic cover:</strong> NZ$7,000 excess and a NZ$3,000 bond.</li>
              <li><strong>NZ$369 total with Peace of Mind:</strong> NZ$1,500 excess and no bond. This is not zero-excess cover.</li>
              <li>Collect at <a href="https://www.gorentals.co.nz/rental-car-locations/queenstown/">Queenstown Airport</a> at 8 AM; return at 6 PM. Arrange the after-hours return in advance.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note">Quote checked 22 September for 17 October only; not held. Includes location and road-care fees. Fuel, optional extras and any payment fees are additional.</p>
            <p class="route">
              <strong>Base route:</strong> Queenstown → Bob’s Cove → Bennett’s Bluff → Glenorchy → Queenstown.
            </p>
            <dl class="option-list">
              <div data-comment-anchor="bobs-cove">
                <dt><a href="https://www.doc.govt.nz/parks-and-recreation/places-to-go/otago/places/queenstown-area/things-to-do/bobs-cove-track-and-nature-walk/">Bob’s Cove &amp; Picnic Point</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">Allow 1–1.5 hours</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Native bush, a lakeside cove and a short, steep climb to the viewpoint. The car park is 14 km from town. Use the marked track; the old bridle track is closed.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="bennetts-bluff">
                <dt><a href="https://www.queenstownnz.co.nz/stories/post/scenic-drives-from-queenstown-explore-more-at-your-own-pace/">Bennett’s Bluff</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">10–15 minutes</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Lake and mountain views, about 25 km from Queenstown. Use the signed lookout car park, not the roadside.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="glenorchy-lagoon">
                <dt><a href="https://www.doc.govt.nz/parks-and-recreation/places-to-go/otago/places/glenorchy-area/things-to-do/glenorchy-walkway/">Glenorchy &amp; Lagoon Walkway</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">Walk: 1–2 hours</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Stop at the red shed and jetty, then follow the wetland boardwalks. Enter from Mull Street, not Glenorchy–Paradise Road. Skip flooded sections. Have lunch in town or bring a picnic.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="routeburn-nature-walk">
                <dt><a href="https://www.doc.govt.nz/parks-and-recreation/places-to-go/otago/places/mount-aspiring-national-park/things-to-do/tracks/routeburn-nature-walk/">Routeburn Nature Walk</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">Optional · 40 min–1 hour</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">An easy beech-forest loop from Routeburn Shelter. Add 35 minutes’ driving each way from Glenorchy, partly on narrow gravel road. Get rental approval first. Choose this instead of the full lagoon walk, not as another compulsory stop.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="note">Queenstown–Glenorchy is about 45 km / 45 minutes each way without stops. Leave Glenorchy around 4 PM for refuelling and the 6 PM vehicle return.</p>
            <details class="booking-notes" data-disclosure-key="glenorchy-booking-notes">
              <DisclosureState />
              <summary>Road restrictions, conditions &amp; cancellation</summary>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Roads:</strong> the base drive uses the sealed Queenstown–Glenorchy Road. <a href="https://www.gorentals.co.nz/terms/">GO’s terms</a> exclude cover on Skippers Road, the road to Macetown, unformed tracks and for water-crossing damage. Public gravel roads are not all excluded, but get written approval for the exact extension and vehicle.</li>
                <li><strong>Paradise:</strong> <a href="https://accessglenorchy.co.nz/paradise/">20 km beyond Glenorchy</a>, with the last 12 km unsealed. Keep it optional, avoid fords, and do not add it on top of Routeburn by default.</li>
                <li><strong>Conditions:</strong> check <a href="https://www.qldc.govt.nz/services/transport-and-parking/winter-road-reports">QLDC road updates</a> and the linked DOC track alerts before departure. October conditions are not yet known. Change the route for flooding, snow, ice or closures.</li>
                <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> more than 24 hours ahead costs 10% of the rental, plus refund administration fees. Less than 24 hours costs 100%. Online cancellation needs at least 48 hours’ notice and adds a 2% refund fee. This is not a fully refundable weather-backup booking.</li>
              </ul>
            </details>
          </PlanSection>

          <PlanSection id="adventures" title="Adventure Day">
            <p>Choose your own activity — the group can split up.</p>
            <p class="note">NZ$ per adult, checked 22 September 2026. Card fees and optional extras are additional.</p>
            <dl class="option-list">
              <div data-comment-anchor="skyline-luge">
                <dt><a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/things-to-do/queenstown-luge/pricing-and-packages/">Skyline Gondola &amp; Luge</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">NZ$99 / 104 / 106</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Gondola + 3 / 5 / 6 luge rides. Gravity-powered carts on downhill tracks, with a chairlift for repeat rides. Six rides cost NZ$742 for all seven people. Unlimited rides: NZ$140 each, unavailable during peak holidays.</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Allow roughly 2–3 hours for six rides and the gondola. <a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/book-now/">Book a luge session</a> and arrive at the gondola base at least 45 minutes beforehand. Published prices; confirm the October date and price when booking.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="shotover-jet">
                <dt><a href="https://www.shotoverjet.com/prices/individual/">Shotover Jet</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">NZ$199</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">25-minute canyon ride with spins, no jump. Allow 1 hour 45 minutes with the free town shuttle.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="ziptrek">
                <dt><a href="https://www.ziptrek.co.nz/tours/moa/">Ziptrek Moa</a> / <a href="https://www.ziptrek.co.nz/tours/kea/">Kea</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">NZ$238 / 288</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Moa: 4 lines, 1.5–2 hours. Kea: 6 lines, 2.5–3 hours. Totals include October tour rates plus the separate <a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/things-to-do/queenstown-gondola/gondola-prices/">NZ$69 gondola ticket</a>. Allow extra time to reach the top.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="kawarau-bungy">
                <dt><a href="https://www.bungy.co.nz/queenstown/kawarau-bungy-centre/kawarau-bridge-bungy/">Kawarau Bridge Bungy</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$320</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">43 m jump. Allow 2.5 hours with the free town bus. Photos and video included; spectators are free.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="nevis-bungy">
                <dt><a href="https://www.bungy.co.nz/queenstown/nevis/nevis-bungy/">Nevis Bungy</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$395</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">134 m jump. Allow 4 hours. Bus, photos, and video included; spectators cost NZ$50.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="skydive">
                <dt><a href="https://www.nzoneskydive.co.nz/prices-deals/">NZONE Skydive</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$379</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">9,000 ft: NZ$379; 12,000 ft: NZ$469; 15,000 ft: NZ$575. Allow about 3.5 hours, with room for delays. Town transport is included; <a href="https://www.nzoneskydive.co.nz/photo-video-packages/">photos/video</a> start at NZ$220 extra.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="note">For skydiving, aim for an early-trip morning and keep a backup day for weather.</p>
            <details class="booking-notes" data-disclosure-key="adventures-booking-notes">
              <DisclosureState />
              <summary>Cancellation &amp; participation rules</summary>
              <ul>
                <li><a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/terms-and-conditions/cancellation-policy/">Skyline Luge</a>: give at least 48 hours’ notice for a cancellation refund. Complete your first ride within the booked 30-minute session; use remaining rides that day. Partial-use refunds follow package differences, not a per-ride rate. <a href="https://queenstown.skyline.co.nz/things-to-do/queenstown-luge/safety/">Helmets and footwear are required</a>; no riding while impaired by alcohol or drugs, or during pregnancy.</li>
                <li><a href="https://www.shotoverjet.com/experience/faqs/">Shotover Jet</a>: 24-hour cancellation policy. Operator weather cancellations offer a refund or reschedule.</li>
                <li><a href="https://www.ziptrek.co.nz/faqs/">Ziptrek</a>: free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour. Maximum weight 125 kg; closed-toe shoes required. Gondola tickets have separate terms.</li>
                <li><a href="https://www.bungy.co.nz/legal/">Bungy</a>: cancel more than 48 hours ahead for a refund, excluding the card fee. Read the weight and health limits for your chosen jump.</li>
                <li><a href="https://www.nzoneskydive.co.nz/terms-conditions/">NZONE</a>: cancel up to 24 hours ahead without a fee. Weather cancellations are rescheduled, or refunded if that is not possible. Harness-fit and health restrictions apply.</li>
              </ul>
            </details>
          </PlanSection>

          <PlanSection id="onsen" anchor="onsen" title="Onsen / Hot Pools">
            <p><a href="https://www.onsen.co.nz/experiences/original-onsen-soak-only/">Original Onsen</a> — 60 minutes, including changing time.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Cost:</strong> two private pools, split 4 + 3. NZ$260 + NZ$225 = <strong>NZ$485 total</strong>, about NZ$69 each if split evenly.</li>
              <li><strong>Transport:</strong> free shuttle from 43 Camp Street. Request it when booking.</li>
              <li><strong>Times seen on 22 September:</strong> Tuesday 13 October at 8:45 PM; Wednesday 14 October at 2:30 PM or 8:45 PM. Two pools and shuttle seats were available together.</li>
              <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> at least 24 hours’ notice for this two-pool booking. <a href="https://www.onsen.co.nz/about/faqs/">Terms &amp; shuttle details</a>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note">Times are local and slots are not held. Towels and water included; bring swimwear.</p>
            <p><a href="https://book.onsen.co.nz/hire/selection?filter=prodgroup-original&amp;workingDate=13-Oct-2026">Check times &amp; book</a></p>
          </PlanSection>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="05" headingId="wine" title="Wine Tasting">
          <p>A Gibbston afternoon by bike, with winery stops and lunch. Prefer the half-day bike tour; use a winery bus instead for poor weather or anyone who does not want to cycle.</p>
  
          <PlanSection id="wine-transport" title="Transport">
            <dl class="option-list">
              <div data-comment-anchor="wine-bike-tour">
                <dt><a href="https://www.aroundthebasin.co.nz/bike-rides/bikewinerieshalfday/">Around The Basin — Bike The Wineries Half Day</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">Preferred · from NZ$105 · allow about 5 hours</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Self-guided riding through Gibbston, with a regular mountain bike or e-bike. Includes Queenstown transfers, helmet, winery map, and trail briefing. Tastings and lunch are extra; the e-bike upgrade price remains unverified.</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Published September–April timetable: check in at the Queenstown shop at 11:50 AM, depart at noon, and start riding from The Church Cellar Door around 12:50 PM. Pickup is at 4:30 PM, followed by the return shuttle. Confirm the meeting point, seven bikes, and shuttle seats for our October date; nothing is booked.</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Explore part of the roughly 9 km wine region rather than riding from Queenstown. The <a href="https://www.queenstowntrail.org.nz/news/news-and-stories/explore-queenstown-trails/">Gibbston River Wine Trail</a> is rated easy / Grade 2, but riders need confidence on gravel and varied terrain. Distance depends on the chosen wineries; an e-bike reduces effort, not the need for bike control.</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Return to The Church, or arrange pickup from another winery on the operator’s map. Call at least 45 minutes before departure to change the pickup. Agree the route and return time before riding; do not plan an evening ride back to town.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="wine-hop-on-hop-off">
                <dt><a href="https://hoponhopoffwinetours.com/products/afternoon-run-queenstown-hop-on-hop-off/">Hop On Hop Off</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">NZ$99.50</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Sunday–Friday: leaves the Station Building on Camp Street at 12:10 PM; the last bus returns around 5:30 PM. Follow the <a href="https://hoponhopoffwinetours.com/maps/queenstown-wine-tour/">timetable</a> between stops. Tastings and lunch are extra.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="wine-hopper-bus">
                <dt><a href="https://www.winehopperbus.co.nz/">Wine Hopper Bus</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$99</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Leaves at noon from 48 Camp Street. The driver arranges pickups between wineries rather than following a fixed loop. Agree your return time on the day. Tastings and lunch are extra.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="note">Wear a helmet and bring water, warm layers, and waterproofs. Use spittoons while cycling and save drinking for the final pickup stop. Never ride impaired. Check spring weather and trail conditions with the operator; do not book both bike and bus transport as required activities.</p>
          </PlanSection>

          <PlanSection id="wineries" title="Winery Shortlist">
            <dl class="option-list">
              <div data-comment-anchor="gibbston-valley-winery">
                <dt><a href="https://www.gibbstonvalley.com/experiences/tours/cave-tour/">Gibbston Valley</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$30</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Classic Cave tour: 30 minutes, three wine tastings, and a visit to the wine cave and historic vines. Choose a scheduled tour that fits the bike route or bus timetable.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="kinross">
                <dt><a href="https://kinross.nz/pages/wine-tasting-experiences">Kinross</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">NZ$30</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">Classic Experience: 45 minutes and five local wines. The cellar door represents five Central Otago producers. A good lunch stop: the bistro serves lunch 11 AM–3 PM; book dining separately from the tasting.</dd>
              </div>
              <div data-comment-anchor="brennan-wines">
                <dt><a href="https://www.brennanwines.com/Visit">Brennan Wines</a></dt>
                <dd class="option-meta">From NZ$45</dd>
                <dd class="option-detail">A vineyard stop with Pinot Noir and less common local varieties. Self-guided flights include three wines. The NZ$65 hosted tasting lasts an hour and includes five wines and appetisers. Open daily, 11 AM–5 PM; book ahead.</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p><strong>Suggested stops:</strong> Gibbston Valley’s cave tour and Kinross for lunch and a tasting. Confirm riding time and lunch service before booking; choose fewer stops rather than rush. Brennan remains an alternative, not an extra required stop. Arrange the shuttle from the final winery.</p>
            <p class="note">Bike package plus the two NZ$30 tastings: from NZ$165 each / NZ$1,155 for seven. The Hop On Hop Off alternative totals NZ$159.50 each / NZ$1,116.50 for seven. These estimates exclude lunch, bottles, and any e-bike upgrade. Book tastings and dining separately for seven; transport does not reserve winery places.</p>
          </PlanSection>
          <PlanSection id="wine-cancellations" title="Cancellation Terms">
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Around The Basin:</strong> <a href="https://www.aroundthebasin.co.nz/terms-and-conditions/">direct-booking terms</a> put seven riders in the 6–14 group: 10% non-refundable deposit, balance due seven days ahead, and full charges for changes or cancellation inside seven days. Weather/refund clauses conflict on 3% versus 10% fees and deposit deductions. Get written confirmation before paying; switching to a bus is not automatically refundable.</li>
              <li><strong>Kinross tasting:</strong> the <a href="https://kinross.nz/pages/classic-wine-tasting">Classic tasting page</a> offers a full refund with more than 24 hours’ notice. Its separate <a href="https://booking.resdiary.com/widget/Standard/KinrossCottages/6655">booking terms</a> list a NZ$15-per-person tasting fee for cancellations with less than 6 hours’ notice, no-shows, or reduced numbers. These terms appear under the groups-of-six-or-more rule. Check which terms apply to the tasting booking.</li>
              <li><strong>Kinross lunch:</strong> the <a href="https://booking.resdiary.com/widget/Standard/KinrossCottages/6655">booking terms</a> require card details for groups of six or more. Dining cancellations with less than 6 hours’ notice, no-shows, or reduced numbers incur NZ$30 per person affected. That is NZ$210 if all seven cancel late. Tables are held for 15 minutes.</li>
              <li><strong>Gibbston Valley:</strong> the <a href="https://www.viator.com/tours/South-Island/Gibbston-Valley-Cave-Tour-w-Transport/d129-38301P3">Viator Cave Tour listing</a> advertises a full refund at least 24 hours before the start. This is the reseller’s policy, not verified direct-booking terms. The direct booking flow requires contact details before the confirmation step; its cancellation deadline remains unverified.</li>
              <li><strong>Brennan Wines:</strong> its <a href="https://booking.resdiary.com/widget/Standard/BrennanWines/12131">booking terms</a> ask for prompt notice of changes to guest numbers, using the confirmation link or a phone call. They do not state a cancellation deadline or fee. That does not establish free cancellation.</li>
              <li><strong>Hop On Hop Off:</strong> <a href="https://hoponhopoffwinetours.com/terms-conditions/">standard tickets</a> are non-refundable within 14 days; cancellations outside that period receive a full refund. Private/group bookings have a 30-day cutoff. The page conflicts on refunds outside that cutoff: one clause promises a full refund; another deducts NZ$200 for private tours. Confirm whether seven standard tickets count as a group booking.</li>
              <li><strong>Wine Hopper Bus:</strong> its <a href="https://www.newzealand.com/us/plan/business/wine-hopper-bus/">Tourism New Zealand listing</a> states a 50% cancellation fee within 48 hours and full payment within 24 hours. Booking-channel terms can differ.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note">Checked 23 September 2026. Bike pricing is an advertised starting rate, not an October quote. Confirm the e-bike price and group refund terms before paying. No bookings made.</p>
          </PlanSection>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="06" headingId="hiking" title="Hiking">
          <p>Suggested pair: Queenstown Hill and Sawpit Gully. Sunshine Bay is the gentler alternative; Tiki Trail is the steeper option.</p>
          <p class="note">Walking times start at the track entrance and exclude travel there. All four options are car-free.</p>
          <dl class="option-list">
            <div data-comment-anchor="queenstown-hill">
              <dt><a href="https://www.queenstownnz.co.nz/stories/post/queenstown-hill-time-walk/">Queenstown Hill</a></dt>
              <dd class="option-meta">2–3 hours hiking · up and back</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Moderate · about 4 km return.</strong> A forest climb to the Basket of Dreams lookout, with views over the lake and mountains. Continue to the summit for a wider view.</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Getting there:</strong> walk uphill from town via Ballarat Street and Kerry Drive to the <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Queenstown%20Hill%20Walking%20Track%20Belfast%20Terrace">Belfast Terrace entrance</a>.</dd>
            </div>
            <div data-comment-anchor="second-hike">
              <dt><a href="https://www.queenstownnz.co.nz/listing/sawpit-gully-trail/2040/">Sawpit Gully, Arrowtown</a></dt>
              <dd class="option-meta">2–3 hours hiking · full loop</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Moderate · 7.9 km loop.</strong> River, forest, old mining remains, and views towards Lake Hayes. Steep sections and creek crossings make this better after dry weather. Leave time for lunch in Arrowtown.</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Getting there:</strong> <a href="https://www.orc.govt.nz/orbus/queenstown-buses/check-your-timetables/4-jacks-point-to-arrowtown-via-queenstown">bus 4 from central Queenstown to Arrowtown</a>, then walk to the track near the <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Arrowtown%20Chinese%20Settlement">Chinese Settlement</a>. Allow extra time for both bus journeys.</dd>
            </div>
            <div data-comment-anchor="sunshine-bay-track">
              <dt><a href="https://www.queenstownnz.co.nz/stories/post/10-beautiful-walks-in-queenstown/">Sunshine Bay Track</a></dt>
              <dd class="option-meta">About 2 hours hiking · out and back</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Easy–moderate · 4 km return.</strong> An undulating bush track beside the lake, ending at Sunshine Bay’s beach and jetty. A good slower-day option without a summit climb.</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Getting there:</strong> start near the <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Sunshine%20Bay%20Track%20Queenstown">Fernhill roundabout</a>, about a 20-minute walk from central Queenstown. Add that approach in both directions.</dd>
            </div>
            <div data-comment-anchor="tiki-trail">
              <dt><a href="https://www.queenstownnz.co.nz/listing/tiki-trail/9099/">Tiki Trail / Skyline</a></dt>
              <dd class="option-meta">2–3 hours hiking · up and back</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Steep · 4.2 km return, about 480 m climb.</strong> A rocky forest track to Skyline’s lake viewpoint. Allow about an hour uphill, plus stops and the descent. Walk down for free, or buy a one-way gondola ticket at the top.</dd>
              <dd class="option-detail"><strong>Getting there:</strong> walk to <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Tiki%20Trail%20Queenstown%20Cemetery%20Road">Cemetery Road, off Brecon Street</a>. The track starts beside the gondola base.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <p class="note">Wear grippy shoes and carry warm, waterproof layers. Check the <a href="https://www.metservice.com/towns-cities/regions/southern-lakes/locations/queenstown">forecast</a> and local track notices before setting off.</p>
        </PlanSection>

        <PlanSection number="07" headingId="unplanned-time" title="Around Queenstown">
          <h3>Pubs &amp; Bars</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Atlas%20Beer%20Cafe%20Queenstown">Atlas Beer Cafe</a> — Craft beer and a steak after a day out.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Smiths%20Craft%20Beer%20House%20Queenstown">Smiths Craft Beer House</a> — Rotating craft beer taps and pub food for a relaxed evening.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Perkys%20Floating%20Bar%20Queenstown">Perky’s Floating Bar</a> — Drinks on a boat, with views across the lake.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Restaurants</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Caribe+Latin+Kitchen/@-45.0327196,168.6639753,15.68z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0xa9d51d8137446061:0xfa7f2cfa82672947!8m2!3d-45.03183!4d168.661404!16s%2Fg%2F11b6qlb1r7?entry=ttu&amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDkyMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D"><strong>Caribe Latin Kitchen</strong></a> — Latin American food for a casual lunch or dinner.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Taco's+Land/@-45.0327196,168.6639753,15.68z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0xa9d51d2f83ef358b:0x2334f9164d184de6!8m2!3d-45.0324213!4d168.6574889!16s%2Fg%2F11m5pnm_ht?entry=ttu&amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDkyMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D"><strong>Taco’s Land</strong></a> — Tacos for an easy meal in town.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Fergburger%20Queenstown">Fergburger</a> — Big takeaway burgers for a casual meal by the lake.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Blue%20Kanu%20Queenstown">Blue Kanu</a> — Pacific and Asian flavours for a sit-down dinner.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Morning Cafés</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Bespoke%20Kitchen%20Queenstown">Bespoke Kitchen</a> — Breakfast and coffee, with plenty of vegetarian and vegan options.</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Vudu%20Cafe%20Larder%20Queenstown">Vudu Café &amp; Larder</a> — A waterfront stop for coffee and a slow brunch.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Something Sweet</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Cookie%20Time%20Cookie%20Bar%20Queenstown">Cookie Time Cookie Bar</a> — Warm cookies and milkshakes when you feel like something sweet.</li>
          </ul>
        </PlanSection>

